1. WHAT THIS COVERS

   The "Work" means all of the following, in source and in built form:

   - the source code of the game engine, the .adv scripting language and its compiler, and the
     tools in tools/ and tests/ (except the third-party software listed in section 4);
   - the story, characters, dialogue, prose, puzzle design, room descriptions, hints and other
     written content under src/content/, docs/ and the game's interface;
   - the painted backgrounds, character art, portraits, props and inventory icons;
   - the music, sound effects and cinematics;
   - the name "The Brass Compass", its title treatment, and the look of its interface.

2. WHAT YOU MAY DO

   You may:

   - play an official build of the game, for personal, non-commercial entertainment;
   - link to the game and to this repository;
   - quote up to 300 words of the game's text, and use screenshots or short capture footage of
     the game, for review, criticism, news coverage, academic discussion or a personal
     playthrough video — provided the game is named and credited and the use is not misleading
     about its origin or licence;
   - keep a local copy of the repository for the purpose of playing, reviewing or building the
     game for your own use, and make the changes needed to run it on your own machine.

3. WHAT YOU MAY NOT DO

   Without prior written permission from the copyright holder, you may not:

   - copy, publish, distribute, sublicense, sell, rent, lease or lend the Work or any build of
     it, in whole or in part;
   - publish modified versions, forks, ports, translations, demakes, remakes or other derivative
     works, or distribute the Work as part of another product;
   - extract, reuse or redistribute the artwork, music, sound effects, cinematics, fonts,
     character designs, names or text as assets, stock, templates or training data;
   - remove or alter this notice, the copyright notice, or the credits in CREDITS.md from any
     copy of the Work;
   - use the Work, its name, or its characters to imply endorsement of another product, or in
     advertising, without permission.

   The permissions in section 2 are the only rights granted. All other rights are reserved.

4. THIRD-PARTY SOFTWARE

   The Work is built with third-party software that remains under its own licence, including
   Vite (MIT) and TypeScript (Apache-2.0); the cinematic source project additionally uses GSAP
   and the HyperFrames toolchain. Their licences govern those components, and nothing in this
   file restricts rights you already have under them. The full list, with links, is in
   CREDITS.md. The game's own content and code are not covered by those licences.

5. AI-GENERATED MATERIAL — PROVENANCE AND DISCLOSURE

   The painted artwork (backgrounds, characters, portraits, props, inventory icons), the music
   and the cinematic footage were produced with generative AI models from the author's prompts
   and direction, then selected, edited, cropped, colour-graded and composed by hand. The game's
   writing — story, characters, dialogue, puzzles, hints, documentation — and all of its code and
   tooling are original work by the author, made with AI-assisted development tools.

   No third-party copyrighted artwork, music, footage or text is knowingly included. The Work is
   not affiliated with, endorsed by, or derived from any existing adventure game or franchise.
   All names, places and events are original.

   To the extent that any jurisdiction does not recognise copyright in machine-generated output,
   the copyright holder claims copyright in the Work as a whole: the selection, arrangement,
   editing, direction and the original human-authored elements. This disclosure is repeated in
   a short, store-ready form in CREDITS.md and docs/STORE.md.

